[center][b]The Commonwealth family: made to work together[/b]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url]: runs the scenes · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url]: NPCs find each other · [b]Overture[/b] (this page): you talk someone into it · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url]: working genitals, arousal and contact · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url]: the physics behind them · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109439]Silhouette[/url]: everyone gets a body of their own · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/fallout4/collections/dmt85e]Ivy's Panties[/url]: all of it, installed for you[/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

Overture is a conversation. Talk to an adult stranger and, once a day, it opens with them before their own dialogue: no hotkey, no menu, no spell. Pick your words, read how they take it, and if you read them right and pick the right place, they may say yes. It is built on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url], which keeps what your words did as the bond between you, and runs the scene if you let it.

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]Four ways to try[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Offer[/b]: caps, a gift, something material.[/*]
[*][b]Charm[/b]: fancy words, patience, a compliment.[/*]
[*][b]Blunt[/b]: crude, direct, explicit.[/*]
[*][b]Linger[/b]: say little, stay, be present.[/*]
[/list]Every NPC is one of four kinds of people, and each way lands with exactly one of them. The game never says who is which: you learn it from how they answer. [b]The place matters too:[/b] in front of more than two people the intimate ways recoil (nothing lost if they'd have liked it), and someone who would say yes answers "not here" until you find somewhere quieter.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@27a7489dfeabf64783d7ff94fdcefe72064d1955/docs/img/flow.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@27a7489dfeabf64783d7ff94fdcefe72064d1955/docs/img/conversation.jpg[/img][/center]

A line that lands opens the next wheel and brings you closer; a miss ends it for the day, and in front of more than two people the intimate ways recoil, while someone who would say yes answers "not here".

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]What you get[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Its own button (0.1.4).[/b] E is always their own talk: their quest, their shop. [b]R, "Overture"[/b], opens a short menu: Try your luck, Follow me, Just talk, Later. Someone who invited you back still opens on E.[/*]
[*][b]0.1.5 and 0.1.6 make the menu work.[/b] Since 0.1.2, R, Follow me and "Ask for a moment" did nothing (the record that tells the game which script to run had one byte too many), and Extended Dialogue Interface hid "Try your luck" and every silent option, Linger and taking their hand, because they have no spoken words. Both are fixed; a safe update.[/*]
[*][b]Every line is voiced.[/b] 236 NPC lines in 11 voices, 5,199 voice files. Characters with their own actor answer in the closest voice we have, through Rapport, for that line only.[/*]
[*][b]You speak too,[/b] in one of two voices designed for this mod, a woman's and a man's, never a copy of any actor. Every option on the wheel comes in five versions, and each conversation picks one, so the same choice doesn't always read or sound the same.[/*]
[*][b]A narrator, not a scoreboard.[/b] After each conversation, one line says what your words did and hints at what to try: another way, another day, somewhere private, after dark. It never names their type.[/*]
[*][b]"Not now" and "not here" are not a no.[/b] Ask again later the same day, or find them somewhere quiet, and it picks up at the question.[/*]
[*][b]"Follow me."[/b] Someone who says "not here" follows you somewhere quieter, and anyone you've warmed up can be asked with "Follow me" on the Overture menu. They keep to their own place: anywhere in their town or settlement, never out of it, and about 60 m in the open. Two game hours without somewhere private, or running off, and they head back. Once you're alone they speak first, and the talk opens at the proposition (new in 0.1.3).[/*]
[*][b]Names for the nameless.[/b] Talk to a Settler or a Drifter and they get a real name, the same one every time you load.[/*]
[*][b]Lovers.[/b] Close enough and after a scene together, you are a couple to everyone. Other people treat them as taken, and your other lovers notice when you are with someone else: some are hurt, some are thrilled.[/*]
[*][b]Orientation is real.[/b] Some people are simply not into your sex. No words and no time will change that, and the narrator tells you so, so you stop trying.[/*]
[*][b]Companions[/b] have a system of their own: days together, fights survived and their own affinity bring you closer, and a companion who wants you may find a moment to say so. You can ask them for a moment too. Works with any companion built on the game's own companion system, and with Amazing Follower Tweaks. Heather Casdin, who runs a system of her own, has her romance counted too (0.1.3).[/*]
[/list][center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@27a7489dfeabf64783d7ff94fdcefe72064d1955/docs/img/askmoment.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Since 0.1.2, "Ask for a moment" appears only where the conversation can open: the same eight checks the conversation makes.[/i][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@a6232c72454030a0e8bb35d0c34ef1fe7d77fe21/docs/img/followme.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]New in 0.1.3: "Follow me" keeps to their own place, all of their town and no further.[/i][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@27a7489dfeabf64783d7ff94fdcefe72064d1955/docs/img/voiced.jpg[/img][/center]

Both sides of every conversation are spoken: 11 voices for the people you approach, two of your own, 5,199 files in all.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@27a7489dfeabf64783d7ff94fdcefe72064d1955/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]

[quote]
[b]"A yes starts a scene" is on by default[/b] (since 0.1.2): when someone says yes, Rapport starts the scene. Switch it off in MCM if you want a yes to be only a yes.

[b]Nothing starts until you leave Vault 111.[/b] No scene and no approach during the game's opening, from character creation to the vault door; alternate starts and MS Skip Prewar Sanctuary work as expected. Using an unusual alternate start that never finishes the opening? MCM, first page, [i]Start now[/i]. [i]Start now[/i] needs Rapport 0.2.2.

[b]Keep the voice files loose.[/b] Don't pack Overture's [font=Courier New]Sound\Voice\Overture.esp[/font] into an archive. Rapport finds a missing recording by looking for the loose file, so packed lines go silent or borrow the wrong voice.

[b]Install with Vortex or MO2; manual installs are not supported.[/b] The installer will not run without Rapport, Extended Dialogue Interface and AAF enabled.

[b]Needs:[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 with F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport 0.2.1[/url] or newer, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/27216]Extended Dialogue Interface[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/31304]AAF[/url]. MCM is optional. With an older Rapport, Overture still runs, without names, lovers or the narrator, and says so once.[/quote][size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]Incompatibilities[/color][/b][/size]

Known conflicts, from real reports and the code. Found another one? Tell us in the Bugs tab.
[list]
[*][b]Heather Casdin[/b]: her romance counts, but moments and "Ask for a moment" are off for her on purpose (her own content is hers).[/*]
[*][b]Ivy[/b]: her own route stays hers on purpose. Overture never opens a conversation with her.[/*]
[*]Nothing else known.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Who can I talk to?[/b]
[spoiler]Adult humans and ghouls, once each per game day. Not anyone who has ever been a companion, who has the companion system instead; not anyone in combat or busy in a scene of their own; not a gen-1 or gen-2 synth.[/spoiler]

[b]Why won't Ivy offer "Ask for a moment"?[/b]
[spoiler]On purpose. Ivy keeps her own route ("Let's make love."), and Overture turns her fade to black into a real Rapport scene when "A yes starts a scene" is on, then hands her back to her own story.[/spoiler]

[b]Is it explicit?[/b]
[spoiler]The crude kind of person talks dirty, on purpose: swearing, teasing, specifically filthy. Everything is between adults and wanted by both. It is an 18+ mod.[/spoiler]

[b]Where is every setting explained?[/b]
[spoiler]In the sticky posts: every MCM setting, what each word is worth, the companion system, and the debug buttons.[/spoiler]

